WEBVTT

00:11.360 --> 00:16.320
Work

00:11.360 --> 00:16.320
Takayuki Yoshii

00:11.360 --> 00:16.320
Masao Takiyama

00:25.790 --> 00:30.760
Original Work/Screenplay

00:25.790 --> 00:30.760
Maya Miyazaki

00:38.510 --> 00:43.480
Director

00:38.510 --> 00:43.480
Takashi Annou

01:27.520 --> 01:39.910
Hotori

01:30.150 --> 01:39.910
I Only Wish for Happiness

02:06.790 --> 02:07.890
School?

02:08.200 --> 02:11.150
Yes, school.
Now, try to remember.

02:11.150 --> 02:12.460
Yes.

02:12.460 --> 02:17.610
In the year 2034 I entered
Wakaba Elementary School.

02:19.110 --> 02:21.790
The teacher of first
grade class 2 at the old

02:21.790 --> 02:24.660
elementary school on top
of the hill was Mizuno-sensei.

02:24.660 --> 02:29.300
She was scary when she was
angry, but her smile was pretty.

02:29.300 --> 02:31.380
I liked her a lot.

02:33.250 --> 02:36.400
But my favorite thing
at school was lunch.

02:36.400 --> 02:40.020
The memories that were inserted
before are successfully implemented.

02:37.350 --> 02:41.140
When I was in third grade,
I went to the fantasy park.

02:50.980 --> 02:54.150
He laughs on his own
when watching cartoons.

02:54.890 --> 02:59.650
Compared to previous sessions, I clearly
see progress, even in this emotion test.

03:01.600 --> 03:02.980
Am I amusing?

03:02.980 --> 03:03.680
What?

03:03.680 --> 03:06.540
Because… when someone laughs
it means he's amused, right?

03:06.860 --> 03:09.040
Yeah, probably…

03:10.560 --> 03:12.540
His understanding of laughter

03:12.540 --> 03:14.590
is limited to an initial stage.

03:22.340 --> 03:24.560
Exercise capabilities test.

03:24.560 --> 03:25.720
Begin.

03:26.080 --> 03:27.090
Okay.

03:32.150 --> 03:35.200
His body's movement
is smooth and natural.

03:35.200 --> 03:37.440
I can see progress
from previous sessions.

03:41.870 --> 03:44.030
Yes? An emergency?

03:45.310 --> 03:47.950
Suzu, I have to go.

03:47.950 --> 03:50.870
At 3 o'clock, go back
to your room as usual.

03:50.870 --> 03:52.870
Yes, I promise.

03:52.870 --> 03:55.040
Promise… yeah.

03:55.040 --> 03:56.090
Keep your promise.

03:56.620 --> 03:57.590
Yes.

05:00.250 --> 05:02.080
It's quiet here…

05:02.800 --> 05:04.220
Brother.

05:10.110 --> 05:11.790
Brother?

05:13.860 --> 05:15.540
It's not Brother?

05:18.710 --> 05:19.790
Um…

05:20.100 --> 05:21.870
I'm not your brother.

05:22.490 --> 05:23.260
Who are you?

05:23.260 --> 05:27.640
I'm Ogura Ryou,
but everyone calls me Suzu.

05:28.850 --> 05:29.930
Suzu…

05:30.260 --> 05:31.210
Yeah.

05:31.210 --> 05:35.930
I got the name Suzu because
it's written the same as Ryou.

05:35.930 --> 05:41.260
I just came to get my ball,
but I heard a voice, so I came…

05:41.260 --> 05:42.600
I'm sorry.

05:43.400 --> 05:44.400
Wait.

05:44.760 --> 05:45.400
Yes.

05:45.900 --> 05:47.410
I'm Hotori.

05:47.410 --> 05:48.960
Shimizu Hotori.

05:48.960 --> 05:51.430
If it's okay with you,
would you stay and talk to me?

05:51.430 --> 05:52.460
Yes.

05:56.580 --> 06:02.800
Until 3 PM, I have 20 minutes
and 10 seconds of free time.

06:02.800 --> 06:04.460
You're pretty punctual.

06:04.460 --> 06:08.300
That's because Usui-san has
taught me to be right on time.

06:08.660 --> 06:12.930
Isn't Usui-san the one in
charge of Personality Plant?

06:12.930 --> 06:15.550
Ah, then… um…

06:16.660 --> 06:18.350
Are you possibly…

06:18.350 --> 06:20.500
Yes, a robot.

06:20.500 --> 06:23.660
So that's why the way
you talk is a little…

06:24.420 --> 06:27.520
But, you look just like a human…

06:27.520 --> 06:30.210
That's how I was made.

06:30.210 --> 06:33.570
This is the first time
I've seen a real one.

06:33.570 --> 06:35.200
Ah, I'm sorry.

06:35.720 --> 06:37.280
Don't apologize.

06:37.280 --> 06:38.210
That's reality.

06:38.610 --> 06:41.850
For saying "real one"… I'm really sorry.

06:41.850 --> 06:43.500
Ah, come in.

06:43.500 --> 06:44.660
Thank you.

06:52.680 --> 06:54.860
Suzu is a pretty name.

06:54.860 --> 06:56.020
Thanks.

06:59.600 --> 07:02.970
But now I'm in the middle of
turning into Ogura Ryou.

07:04.060 --> 07:07.860
A person named Ogura Ryou-kun's
personality is being inserted into you?

07:07.860 --> 07:08.600
Yeah.

07:08.600 --> 07:13.160
Every time they insert more
information, I gain more memories.

07:17.850 --> 07:20.160
So the memories are flowing in…

07:20.160 --> 07:21.670
Yeah, they are.

07:21.670 --> 07:24.830
Usui-san always does tests
to see if the memories

07:24.830 --> 07:26.750
and personality are implemented or not.

07:31.420 --> 07:32.640
The opposite of me.

07:33.890 --> 07:35.650
You know…

07:35.650 --> 07:37.080
I have an illness.

07:37.080 --> 07:38.410
It's a disease…

07:41.470 --> 07:44.050
that makes my memories
slip out of my mind.

07:44.050 --> 07:45.900
Memories… Mind…

07:48.390 --> 07:49.420
Umm…

07:50.100 --> 07:51.910
why don't you have them do
to you what they do to me?

07:54.080 --> 07:58.620
Why don't you have them insert
artificial memories like what I have?

08:00.310 --> 08:01.120
It's impossible.

08:01.680 --> 08:06.410
I'm human, artificial memories
can't be inserted into me.

08:17.680 --> 08:18.670
But…

08:18.670 --> 08:21.400
it would have been great
if I really could have them.

08:25.630 --> 08:28.690
He's still not ready to meet you.

08:28.690 --> 08:32.020
However, I think it would be good
to show you the progress.

08:38.460 --> 08:39.030
Here.

08:39.030 --> 08:40.290
Usui-san, you are not eating?

08:40.610 --> 08:43.430
Yes, I've already eaten lunch.

08:43.430 --> 08:44.870
Thank you for the food.

08:50.430 --> 08:51.550
Does it taste good?

08:52.270 --> 08:53.730
Tastes great!

08:54.950 --> 08:56.590
I love Doria.

08:57.600 --> 08:58.600
Aren't you eating that?

08:58.980 --> 09:01.620
I hate green peas.

09:02.590 --> 09:03.430
Ryou!

09:03.430 --> 09:04.540
It's Ryou…

09:04.540 --> 09:08.770
That kid… I always told him
he can't leave the green peas…

09:12.200 --> 09:15.980
I'm sure you understand,
but you can't expect too much.

09:15.980 --> 09:17.430
Ah… yes.

09:17.430 --> 09:20.790
The technology of inserting
artificial personalities is limited.

09:20.790 --> 09:24.900
We can't possibly make a perfect
copy of Ryou-kun's personality.

09:24.900 --> 09:27.880
No matter how much they're
alike, he's just a robot.

09:27.880 --> 09:30.880
He's nothing more than a doll imitation.

09:31.210 --> 09:33.380
Yes… we understand, Doctor.

09:33.380 --> 09:34.230
But…

09:36.110 --> 09:38.410
A doll's imitation is enough.

09:38.410 --> 09:42.930
We want to feel his
presence, even a little bit.

09:43.470 --> 09:47.600
That's why… when you found out
Ryou had an incurable disease…

09:47.600 --> 09:50.820
you requested this from the
Artificial Personality Committee.

09:52.320 --> 09:57.200
I want Ryou to always be with us,
even if it's only one percent of him…

09:57.590 --> 09:59.990
I understand your feelings.

10:01.820 --> 10:03.450
Very well…

10:24.050 --> 10:26.540
This is a really dark
and dusty place, huh?

10:26.540 --> 10:30.440
This area hasn't been used
by anyone for a long time.

10:47.960 --> 10:48.630
Suzu.

10:49.460 --> 10:51.060
Don't tell anyone, okay?

10:51.060 --> 10:51.980
Tell what?

10:51.980 --> 10:53.500
Just promise me.

10:53.500 --> 10:55.150
I know this, pinky swear.

10:55.150 --> 10:56.000
Yes.

10:56.000 --> 10:58.130
Promise me to protect the secret.

11:00.480 --> 11:02.640
Okay, I promise.

11:26.020 --> 11:27.110
You know…

11:27.110 --> 11:29.210
My secret place…

11:29.620 --> 11:31.210
Secret place?

11:32.250 --> 11:35.290
I'll only show it to you.

11:41.960 --> 11:43.220
What is this place?

11:45.110 --> 11:46.750
An old greenhouse.

11:47.420 --> 11:49.670
A place everyone has forgotten.

11:56.190 --> 11:57.960
A place no one will visit.

11:59.620 --> 12:02.830
That's why I come here…

12:02.830 --> 12:05.880
when I'm sad, or don't know what to do,

12:05.880 --> 12:07.440
or am tired,

12:07.440 --> 12:09.910
or when my heart hurts.

12:09.910 --> 12:11.500
Your heart hurts?

12:12.060 --> 12:13.370
Sometimes.

12:15.100 --> 12:19.450
Hey, this place is a secret
from Brother and Papa, okay?

12:19.450 --> 12:20.600
Only Suzu.

12:20.600 --> 12:22.480
You're the only one I've told.

12:22.480 --> 12:24.390
Thank you for telling me.

12:29.280 --> 12:31.140
It's pretty…

12:31.140 --> 12:32.920
I got them from Mama.

12:32.920 --> 12:36.500
Mama told me she got them from
Grandma when she was small.

12:42.670 --> 12:44.080
Mama… she died.

12:44.080 --> 12:45.340
Died?

12:45.340 --> 12:48.250
When I was six years old,
in a car accident.

12:48.250 --> 12:50.160
A car accident?

12:50.160 --> 12:54.560
Playing with these marbles
with Mama was fun…

12:55.410 --> 12:59.670
Mama used to say, "Hey, look, Hotori."

13:00.170 --> 13:04.680
"In each marble there's a
reflection of Hotori and Mama."

13:11.230 --> 13:15.750
Mama smelled better than soap and candy…

13:15.750 --> 13:22.690
When she hugged me… I got a kind of…
happy feeling surrounding me.

13:25.610 --> 13:26.750
But…

13:26.750 --> 13:28.550
it will all disappear.

13:30.050 --> 13:33.290
These memories of Mama, will all…

13:34.800 --> 13:39.460
disappear together with
the rest of my memories.

13:39.460 --> 13:41.380
Hotori…

13:41.980 --> 13:43.280
I'm sorry…

13:45.630 --> 13:47.390
Suzu can't understand that, huh?

13:47.390 --> 13:49.390
Yes, I don't understand.

13:51.930 --> 13:53.890
But I want to understand.

13:54.280 --> 13:55.530
I want to understand…

13:57.010 --> 13:59.400
I want to understand Hotori better.

14:50.950 --> 14:53.450
Then… the keyword is skiing.

14:53.450 --> 14:56.670
I learned skiing from my dad.

14:56.670 --> 14:59.810
Dad is a really good skier.

14:59.810 --> 15:03.210
It's a secret, but Mom isn't very good.

15:05.340 --> 15:08.420
The implementation of the
memories is very stable,

15:08.420 --> 15:10.720
and his speech is remarkably smooth.

15:12.880 --> 15:14.700
Usui-san, are you happy?

15:14.700 --> 15:15.430
What?

15:16.080 --> 15:19.410
Maybe because I'm progressing?

15:19.410 --> 15:21.440
That's right, Suzu. I'm happy.

15:22.920 --> 15:25.900
He is also starting to
understand laughter better.

15:35.380 --> 15:36.410
Suzu?

15:36.410 --> 15:38.090
You didn't come yesterday, so…

15:39.450 --> 15:40.510
Brother.

15:40.510 --> 15:42.040
Who's Suzu?

15:42.980 --> 15:43.890
A friend.

15:43.890 --> 15:46.340
So you made a friend… a patient kid?

15:47.010 --> 15:49.150
Well… Suzu is a robot.

15:50.550 --> 15:52.270
From Personality Plant.

15:52.270 --> 15:54.270
I see. A robot.

15:54.270 --> 15:58.040
He's a really good kid,
and he's almost like a human…

16:01.760 --> 16:03.650
Saying that is awful…

16:05.610 --> 16:06.790
You know,

16:15.690 --> 16:16.860
Hotori…

16:18.700 --> 16:20.830
Hotori! Hotori!

16:20.830 --> 16:21.830
Hotori!

16:22.180 --> 16:22.830
It hurts!

16:24.180 --> 16:25.120
Sorry.

16:33.640 --> 16:35.350
Brother, when did you come?

16:39.040 --> 16:40.120
Hello.

16:40.120 --> 16:41.770
Suzu, come in.

16:42.930 --> 16:44.730
Brother's here too.

16:56.890 --> 16:58.570
Did anything happen?

16:58.570 --> 16:59.920
You look pale…

17:04.500 --> 17:05.780
Can it be…

17:05.780 --> 17:07.770
"If you want to see
my cute little sister,

17:07.770 --> 17:11.210
you have to get my permission
first, so go away"…?

17:14.000 --> 17:15.040
Um…

17:15.040 --> 17:17.030
was that wrong of me to say?

17:20.300 --> 17:23.560
No, that was good.
You're better than normal humans.

17:24.620 --> 17:26.030
Thank you, Suzu-kun.

17:26.030 --> 17:27.950
For becoming Hotori's friend.

17:27.950 --> 17:30.980
Don't thank me.
I also enjoy being with Hotori.

17:30.980 --> 17:34.200
Um… when I talk to Hotori,

17:34.200 --> 17:37.680
my heart feels very warm.

17:37.680 --> 17:39.480
Oh, I'm glad.

17:40.650 --> 17:42.400
Hotori, I'll come again.

17:42.400 --> 17:44.360
Okay, Brother.

17:44.360 --> 17:46.400
I'm fine now.

17:46.400 --> 17:47.880
My health condition is good.

17:48.310 --> 17:50.420
Because I have fun all the time.

17:50.420 --> 17:51.490
That's great.

17:51.490 --> 17:53.130
Later.

17:53.470 --> 17:54.630
Yeah.

18:07.650 --> 18:09.070
What's wrong?

18:09.780 --> 18:11.030
Nothing.

18:11.030 --> 18:14.280
But you just sighed and
shrugged your shoulders.

18:14.280 --> 18:15.570
I wonder why…

18:15.570 --> 18:17.910
I can't smile well in front of you.

18:17.910 --> 18:21.020
Maybe I am incapable of
smiling when I am with you.

18:23.870 --> 18:25.660
In front of my brother…

18:26.510 --> 18:28.450
I can still smile nicely.

18:28.450 --> 18:31.170
"Can smile nicely"… What does that mean?

18:36.320 --> 18:38.760
It's because I don't
want to make him worry.

18:41.090 --> 18:45.180
My brother often worries about me.

18:45.740 --> 18:51.530
I don't want to make him more
worried and upset than he is already.

18:54.010 --> 18:57.500
If I always show him a nice smile,

18:57.500 --> 19:00.820
I won't make Brother too worried.

19:00.820 --> 19:01.470
Don't you think so?

19:01.470 --> 19:02.780
Hotori, that's just weird!

19:04.730 --> 19:09.670
Smiling is something people do
when they're amused or happy.

19:14.670 --> 19:17.670
Yeah… you're right.

19:20.030 --> 19:23.910
But humans aren't always like that.

19:26.910 --> 19:29.440
Sometimes they smile
even when they're sad.

19:29.440 --> 19:31.090
She's right…

19:31.090 --> 19:33.360
Hotori smiles even though she looks sad…

19:39.140 --> 19:40.200
So you came.

19:40.200 --> 19:41.450
Father.

19:41.450 --> 19:42.680
Hotori…

19:43.370 --> 19:44.270
Hotori…

19:44.270 --> 19:46.950
Her symptoms are increasing.

19:50.190 --> 19:51.620
Yes.

19:51.620 --> 19:52.980
So you've noticed it too, Tatsuki…

19:52.980 --> 19:54.030
You knew.

19:54.030 --> 19:55.360
Then, Personality Plant…

19:55.360 --> 19:56.710
I won't use Personality Plant.

19:57.940 --> 20:01.470
I've decided not to use
Personality Plant.

20:01.470 --> 20:02.590
But!

20:03.040 --> 20:08.550
Even if we do it, she can only be
a doll imitation with no soul.

20:08.550 --> 20:11.800
I don't want Hotori to be in that form.

20:11.800 --> 20:14.070
But… even if it's a robot…

20:14.070 --> 20:16.010
it's pretty close to a real human.

20:16.010 --> 20:16.610
Tatsuki!

20:18.310 --> 20:20.090
This conversation is over.

20:20.090 --> 20:21.490
You really are confused.

20:23.620 --> 20:25.870
Because you're confused,
you started preparing…

20:25.870 --> 20:28.860
an artificial copy of Hotori's
personality, but didn't finish it!

20:51.740 --> 20:52.980
Hotori…

20:54.440 --> 20:56.020
What should Papa do?

21:31.280 --> 21:32.750
Ryou!

21:34.520 --> 21:37.940
Hurry and finish learning…

21:37.940 --> 21:41.430
and return to Papa and Mama…

21:44.870 --> 21:46.870
It's weird.

21:48.650 --> 21:51.160
Because I'm Ogura Ryou,

21:51.160 --> 21:55.260
if Father and Mother
call me Ryou and hug me…

21:55.260 --> 21:57.340
I'm supposed to be happy.

21:57.340 --> 21:58.650
But…

21:59.390 --> 22:01.550
I wasn't really happy.

22:02.920 --> 22:05.470
Not that I disliked it…

22:05.470 --> 22:07.850
but I felt kind of weird.

22:11.970 --> 22:14.980
Sometimes I don't know…

22:14.980 --> 22:17.600
who I am.

22:18.480 --> 22:21.360
When additional information is inserted,

22:21.360 --> 22:24.820
memories that weren't there
yesterday sneak into my head.

22:31.440 --> 22:34.400
Things I didn't know yesterday,

22:34.400 --> 22:37.210
feel like I've always known them today.

22:38.450 --> 22:40.360
I really don't understand…

22:40.960 --> 22:43.060
What are these memories?

22:43.060 --> 22:44.840
Ryou's memories?

22:44.840 --> 22:47.000
Suzu's memories?

22:47.000 --> 22:49.030
Which one of them is here right now?

22:49.030 --> 22:50.270
Ryou?

22:50.270 --> 22:51.270
Suzu?

22:53.970 --> 22:55.060
Suzu!

22:55.060 --> 22:57.300
Suzu, are you okay?

23:00.750 --> 23:02.500
Isn't it weird?

23:02.500 --> 23:05.070
Even though Ryou and Suzu
are the same person…

23:06.720 --> 23:10.720
Suzu was born in order to become Ryou.

23:11.900 --> 23:13.130
But…

23:13.130 --> 23:15.540
I don't feel like that.

23:17.020 --> 23:18.720
Even if I start thinking about it…

23:18.720 --> 23:20.420
there's nothing I can do.

23:25.580 --> 23:27.380
Totally opposite, huh?

23:28.820 --> 23:29.930
You and me…

23:33.380 --> 23:39.120
Memories that aren't supposed to
be there, flow into you and gather.

23:40.620 --> 23:45.780
Memories that I'm supposed to have,
keep leaving me and disappear…

23:49.130 --> 23:50.950
I can't remember…

23:51.250 --> 23:52.740
Mama's face.

23:55.500 --> 23:58.620
Even though I remembered that yesterday.

23:58.620 --> 24:02.000
I'm going to just keep
forgetting everything like this.

24:02.690 --> 24:04.680
Mama's warmth too.

24:04.680 --> 24:09.080
The shooting star I saw in the middle
of the night when I couldn't sleep.

24:09.080 --> 24:12.430
The taste of the ice cream
I ate with Brother.

24:12.430 --> 24:18.220
The snow rabbit that Papa made
for me one snowy morning.

24:21.140 --> 24:23.280
All those precious memories…

24:23.280 --> 24:26.730
If I lose all of my
memories, I won't be…

24:29.530 --> 24:30.740
myself anymore.

24:30.740 --> 24:32.840
That's not true!

24:32.840 --> 24:34.370
I'm scared.

24:34.910 --> 24:38.150
The truth is that I'm very scared.

24:38.150 --> 24:39.630
I'm scared…

24:39.630 --> 24:40.920
So scared…

24:40.920 --> 24:43.370
So scared that I can't stand it!

24:43.370 --> 24:44.900
Hotori!

24:44.900 --> 24:46.910
I'm here with you!

24:46.910 --> 24:49.370
I'm… I'm…

25:08.440 --> 25:11.010
Suzu, I have a favor to ask of you.

25:11.010 --> 25:12.010
Hmm?

25:12.010 --> 25:14.000
Something I want you to promise.

25:14.000 --> 25:14.870
Okay.

25:14.870 --> 25:16.790
I'll promise anything.

25:25.310 --> 25:27.480
I found this here earlier.

25:33.880 --> 25:37.520
I think someone hid it
here a long time ago.

25:37.520 --> 25:38.560
What?

25:41.120 --> 25:42.890
Shoot me with this.

25:47.550 --> 25:51.230
If I lose my memories and my mind,

25:51.230 --> 25:54.490
and forget who I am, and forget you…

25:55.160 --> 25:56.900
shoot me with this.

25:58.670 --> 25:59.720
Hotori!

25:59.720 --> 26:01.430
You promised, didn't you?

26:01.430 --> 26:05.060
Promises must be kept no matter what.

26:06.000 --> 26:07.210
Please.

26:24.920 --> 26:28.810
Why did I make that promise…

26:29.340 --> 26:31.920
Why did I…

26:30.380 --> 26:31.680
Ryou?

26:31.680 --> 26:33.190
Ryou-kun?

26:36.070 --> 26:37.330
Ryou-kun?

26:37.910 --> 26:39.240
Ryou-kun?

26:40.020 --> 26:40.680
Suzu.

26:41.510 --> 26:42.460
What?

26:42.460 --> 26:43.700
What is it, Usui-san?

26:44.260 --> 26:45.410
Weird…

26:45.410 --> 26:46.900
What is it?

26:46.900 --> 26:48.420
What did you want, Usui-san?

26:48.950 --> 26:53.340
The inserted memory
is already up to 95%.

26:54.510 --> 26:56.420
So, why?

26:57.220 --> 26:58.930
Usui-san, what's wrong?

26:59.240 --> 27:00.930
Suzu…

27:00.930 --> 27:04.430
Why don't you respond
when Ryou is called?

27:09.450 --> 27:10.700
Why…

27:24.580 --> 27:25.920
Brother!

27:26.850 --> 27:28.050
Suzu!

27:28.050 --> 27:28.850
Hotori…

27:28.850 --> 27:30.600
Have you seen Hotori?

27:30.600 --> 27:32.480
Is Hotori gone?!

27:32.480 --> 27:35.500
Maybe the symptoms appeared again…

27:35.500 --> 27:36.630
I'll search for her!

27:36.630 --> 27:37.630
Please do!

27:39.850 --> 27:43.140
Please do… I'll go tell Father.

27:56.760 --> 27:58.070
Hotori!

27:59.010 --> 28:00.640
Hotori!

28:04.950 --> 28:06.300
Hotori!

28:07.940 --> 28:09.810
Hotori!

28:20.290 --> 28:21.340
Hotori…

28:55.170 --> 28:56.090
Hotori…

29:03.560 --> 29:04.680
Hotori!

29:04.980 --> 29:06.680
Hotori!!

29:22.220 --> 29:24.770
Don't move, Hotori…

30:08.910 --> 30:12.330
Hotori, why did you do
something so dangerous?

30:20.650 --> 30:22.340
Who are you?

30:52.230 --> 30:53.430
I…

30:54.800 --> 30:55.770
Hotori.

31:00.630 --> 31:04.160
I see… I had a big attack.

31:04.160 --> 31:05.010
Hotori,

31:05.010 --> 31:06.710
it's okay…

31:06.710 --> 31:08.760
Papa is here now.

31:09.570 --> 31:11.570
The promised time has come.

31:13.040 --> 31:14.770
Please… Suzu.

31:20.340 --> 31:23.160
Hotori? What happened to Hotori?

31:23.160 --> 31:25.280
She's fine. Looks like she woke up.

31:25.910 --> 31:28.720
Dr. Shimizu and her
brother are with her.

31:29.300 --> 31:30.700
I see…

31:32.010 --> 31:33.010
I'm glad…

31:33.010 --> 31:34.670
Really glad…

31:40.110 --> 31:41.640
Suzu…

31:41.640 --> 31:43.290
You really are…

31:43.970 --> 31:44.800
Impossible!

31:45.630 --> 31:49.260
For a Personality Plant robot
to develop a personality of his own…

31:49.260 --> 31:51.300
But Suzu…

31:51.750 --> 31:53.600
He's not a copy of Ryou-kun.

31:53.600 --> 31:56.310
He has a personality as Suzu.

31:56.310 --> 31:58.310
You're right…

31:58.640 --> 32:00.230
I wonder what will happen…

32:01.940 --> 32:02.720
Suzu…

32:02.720 --> 32:05.430
The Oguras own Suzu.

32:05.430 --> 32:09.910
If the Oguras can't
accept Suzu in this state…

32:14.630 --> 32:16.010
That child…

32:16.010 --> 32:17.830
You'll erase Suzu, huh?

32:27.700 --> 32:29.790
Wow, fireworks!

32:29.790 --> 32:31.130
Pretty, huh?

34:44.510 --> 34:45.940
I can't do it…

34:46.640 --> 34:48.310
There's no way I could do it…

34:56.960 --> 35:00.470
I want you, Hotori, to stay with me.

35:01.240 --> 35:02.710
Even if your memories are gone…

35:02.710 --> 35:04.690
and your mind is gone…

35:04.690 --> 35:06.670
Hotori is Hotori.

35:18.160 --> 35:20.970
I exist inside of this.

35:51.500 --> 35:55.920
Naze kimi wa iru no

35:51.500 --> 35:55.920
Why do you exist?

35:54.530 --> 35:55.790
Thank you,

35:55.790 --> 35:58.220
for always being Hotori's friend.

35:57.390 --> 36:01.960
Naze koko ni iru no

35:57.390 --> 36:01.960
Why are you here?

35:58.220 --> 36:01.670
I want to say thank you
to Hotori for that as well.

36:01.670 --> 36:02.490
Yes.

36:02.490 --> 36:05.290
And, Hotori wants to tell you thank you

36:03.790 --> 36:13.780
Haruka na seikoku yo hokori kakeru

36:03.790 --> 36:13.780
Risking your pride on a distant goal…

36:05.290 --> 36:10.230
for the snow rabbit you made
for her on that snowy morning.

36:13.230 --> 36:15.570
Hotori is in my heart.

36:14.680 --> 36:19.480
Naze boku wa iru no

36:14.680 --> 36:19.480
Why do I exist?

36:15.570 --> 36:18.200
Yes, Hotori is kept in my heart too.

36:18.200 --> 36:20.140
Come to play at any time.

36:20.500 --> 36:25.320
Naze kimi to iru no

36:20.500 --> 36:25.320
Why am I with you?

36:20.740 --> 36:22.240
Okay.

36:26.700 --> 36:39.270
Hara no hiruma wa ima yomigaeru

36:26.700 --> 36:39.270
The wild days have returned.

36:28.020 --> 36:30.100
That's dangerous, Suzu!

36:30.830 --> 36:32.690
Have you said goodbye to everyone?

36:32.690 --> 36:33.250
Yeah.

36:34.030 --> 36:36.750
Then let's go home.
Hurry and get in, Suzu.

36:37.090 --> 36:38.260
Yes.

36:40.690 --> 36:46.270
Kimi ga warau kimi no omou

36:40.690 --> 36:46.270
Thinking of you laughing…

36:45.180 --> 36:47.470
Is it okay not to tell your father?

36:46.680 --> 36:51.770
Sore wa taisetsu

36:46.680 --> 36:51.770
that is valuable.

36:47.470 --> 36:51.440
That you are really in my heart?

36:51.440 --> 36:52.860
It's okay.

36:52.370 --> 36:55.180
Kimi ga ikiru

36:52.370 --> 36:55.180
You live,

36:52.860 --> 36:59.490
I'm sure Papa and Brother will be
okay without knowing I'm with you.

36:55.260 --> 36:58.150
Koko ni ikiru

36:55.260 --> 36:58.150
live here.

36:58.370 --> 37:03.760
Sore ga yakusoku

36:58.370 --> 37:03.760
That is the promise,

36:59.900 --> 37:01.560
Humans are a mystery.

37:01.560 --> 37:02.990
They are?

37:02.990 --> 37:05.990
Even though Hotori's artificial
personality is inside of me…

37:04.440 --> 37:09.170
Towa no yakusoku

37:04.440 --> 37:09.170
the eternal promise.

37:07.170 --> 37:14.920
Why did your father and brother say
that you were in their hearts too?

37:15.880 --> 37:18.120
It's not artificial personality, but…

37:18.120 --> 37:22.180
I'm there in Papa's and
Brother's hearts too.

37:23.010 --> 37:24.830
Hmm? Weird.

37:24.830 --> 37:25.950
That's right.

37:25.950 --> 37:27.650
Humans are weird.

37:55.830 --> 38:00.340
Nani wo sagashiteru no

37:55.830 --> 38:00.340
What are you looking for?

38:01.500 --> 38:06.240
Doko e kimi wa yuku no

38:01.500 --> 38:06.240
Where are you going to?

38:07.840 --> 38:18.400
Haruka na negai yo futo uzuki dasu

38:07.840 --> 38:18.400
A distant wish, suddenly begins to ache.

38:18.970 --> 38:23.740
Dakara koko ni deai

38:18.970 --> 38:23.740
That's why we meet here,

38:24.790 --> 38:29.760
Nani ka hibiki yoiru

38:24.790 --> 38:29.760
making some sounds.

38:31.050 --> 38:44.340
Michi no tobira wa ima hirakareru

38:31.050 --> 38:44.340
The door to the path is now open…

38:45.050 --> 38:50.740
Kimi ga warau kimi ga omou

38:45.050 --> 38:50.740
Thinking of you laughing…

38:50.860 --> 38:56.300
Sore wa taisetsu

38:50.860 --> 38:56.300
that is valuable.

38:56.680 --> 38:59.490
Kimi ga ikiru

38:56.680 --> 38:59.490
You live,

38:59.580 --> 39:02.600
Koko ni ikiru

38:59.580 --> 39:02.600
live here.

39:02.850 --> 39:07.790
Sore ga yakusoku

39:02.850 --> 39:07.790
That is the promise.

39:08.400 --> 39:11.100
Meguri aeru

39:08.400 --> 39:11.100
Meeting by chance,

39:11.320 --> 39:14.000
Musubi aeru

39:11.320 --> 39:14.000
and being tied together.

39:14.040 --> 39:19.390
Sore wa taisetsu

39:14.040 --> 39:19.390
That is valuable.

39:19.910 --> 39:22.690
Koko ni ikiru

39:19.910 --> 39:22.690
Living here,

39:22.790 --> 39:25.840
Ima wo ikiru

39:22.790 --> 39:25.840
living now.

39:26.060 --> 39:31.200
Sore ga yakusoku

39:26.060 --> 39:31.200
That is the promise.

39:31.970 --> 39:37.200
Towa no yakusoku

39:31.970 --> 39:37.200
The eternal promise.

39:37.660 --> 39:39.650
Sore ga…

39:37.660 --> 39:39.650
That is…

39:49.700 --> 39:54.620
Director

39:49.700 --> 39:54.620
Takashi Annou

39:55.200 --> 40:00.170
Production

39:55.200 --> 40:00.170
Sunrise

39:55.200 --> 40:00.170
Animax Broadcast Japan
